    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/enmu/jobs/5087924/assistant-professor-of-nursing": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Nursing",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Nursing Salary Depends on Qualifications Location Main Campus - Portales, NM Job Type Full time permanent Job Number 2025-00147 Department Academic Affairs Division College of Liberal Arts and Sciences Opening Date 09/22/2025 Description Benefits Questions Position Overview Position Summary: Eastern New Mexico University’s (ENMU) Department of Health and Human Services invites applications for a full-time tenure-track Assistant Professor of Nursing. The position entails a 4/4 teaching load. This is a residential appointment in a collegial department with a supportive campus culture, and campus presence/relocation is required. ENMU seeks candidates committed to excellent undergraduate and graduate education and student success within the framework of the teacher-scholar model. Requirements Duties and Responsibilities: Under the direction of the Nursing Program Director Provide online BSN and MSN level instruction support to nursing students and the nursing program. Advisement and mentoring. Research and other scholarly activities are expected The faculty member will be expected to assist with ACEN accreditation compliance as assigned Recruitment and Retention duties. Contribute to academic planning, curricular design, program development, recruiting/retention efforts, and program assessment. Serve on departmental, college and university committees. Attend departmental and university faculty meetings and external meetings as required Regular and predictable attendance is required Perform other appropriate duties as assigned by the Nursing Director and/or as outlined in the Faculty Handbook. Minimum Job Requirements: Doctorate or ABD required. Graduate degree in Nursing required. Nursing education certification with online teaching experience preferred. Candidate must be eligible for New Mexico RN licensure. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Must possess strong interpersonal and communication skills Must possess strong commitment to excellence in teaching students of diverse backgrounds. Must have the skills to design, deliver, and manage online learning courses using a Learning Management System. Working Conditions Physical Demand and Working Conditions: Work is generally sedentary in nature. The job may require exerting up to 10 pounds of force occasionally and/or a consistent amount of force frequently or constantly to lift, carry, push, pull, or otherwise move objects. Essential Functions: [ As defined under the Americans with Disabilities Act, these include the aforementioned duties and responsibilities, minimum job requirements, knowledge, skills, and abilities, and physical demand and working conditions. This is not necessarily an all-inclusive listing.] Additional Information Condition of Employment: Must pass a pre-employment background check. Electronic Application Instructions: Electronic applications should be submitted through the \"Apply\" link on the top of this page. Please attach the following required documents to your electronic application. Required Documents: Letter of interest Curriculum vitae Contact information for three references (blind or off list reference checks may be conducted on finalists) Transcripts (unofficial for application purposes) Equal Employment Opportunity /Title IX/IPRA. Eastern New Mexico University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, sex (including pregnancy, gender identity, and sexual orientation), age, disability, genetic information, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected under federal, state, or local laws. If a reasonable accommodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process, or to perform essential job functions, please contact the Office of Human Resources at (575) 562-2115. New Mexico is an open records state; therefore, ENMU complies with the Inspection of Public Records Act, NMSA 1978, Chapter 14, Article 2, from the Office of the New Mexico Attorney General. Any concerns regarding sex discrimination should be addressed to the Title IX Coordinator at either titleix.coordinator@enmu.eu , (575) 562-2235, or Curry Hall Office 127, 1500 S Avenue K, Portales, NM 88130. Requests for inspection of public records should be sent to planning.analysis@enmu.edu . For any other inquiries, please contact Human Resources at (575) 562-2115 or e-mail ENMU.HRrecruiter@enmu.edu . ENMU uses E-Verify to confirm the employment eligibility of all newly hired employees. To learn more about E-Verify, including your rights and responsibilities, please visit www.dhs.gov/E-Verify. . Insurance Insurance for Eastern New Mexico University is offered through the New Mexico Public Schools Insurance Authority . High coverage and low coverage options are offered for medical and dental insurance so employees can choose the plan that’s right for them. Health insurance is offered through both Blue Cross and Blue Shield of New Mexico and the Presbyterian Health Plan Dental insurance is offered through United Concordia , Delta Dental , and Blue Cross Blue Shield Dental Vision insurance is offered through Davis Vision . Life insurance is offered through Standard Life Insurance Company and UNUM Life Insurance Company . Retirement Eastern New Mexico University participates with the New Mexico Educational Retirement Board (NMERB) , Social Security , and Medicare . The University also offers supplemental retirement plans. 403b and 457b plans are available through TIAA/CREF , AIG VALIC , Roth 403b and 457b plans are also available through TIAA/CREF . Paid Time Off Faculty will receive 5 personal days a year and 48 hours a semester for sick leave. Employee Educational Assistance Plan Eastern New Mexico University offers a tuition waiver for regular employees and retirees. This program waives the tuition for three courses (up to nine credit hours) per semester. Employees' spouses or children may be eligible to use the tuition waiver during any semester that it is not being used by the employee. 01 How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Albuquerque Journal Amarillo Globe News Chronicle of Higher Education Clovis News Journal ENMU Website Lubbock Avalanche Portales News Tribune Ruidoso News Roswell Daily Records Alamogordo Daily News Professional Journal www.enmjobfinder.com www.higheredjobs.com www.monster.com www.Indeed.com www.highplainshelpwanted.com Other Required Question Employer Eastern New Mexico University Address 1500 S. Ave. K, Station 21 Portales, New Mexico, 88130 Phone 575-562-2115 Website http://www.enmu.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/enmu/jobs/5275003/assistant-professor-of-management": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Management",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Management Salary Depends on Qualifications Location Main Campus - Portales, NM Job Type Full time permanent Job Number 2026-00045 Department Academic Affairs Division College of Business Opening Date 03/18/2026 Description Benefits Questions Position Overview Position Summary The College of Business at Eastern New Mexico University is an ACBSP accredited school that seeks candidates for a full-time tenure track position as an Assistant Professor of Management. The college provides quality, student focused business education preparing individuals for professional careers, graduate studies, and lifelong learning. Candidates must be able to teach production and operations management at the undergraduate and graduate level; preference will be given to candidates who can also teach in other areas of business. This is a residential appointment starting in January 2027, with the candidate expected to relocate to the Portales, New Mexico area. Requirements Duties and Responsibilities: This position may require additional teaching responsibilities. Faculty responsibilities include: Teach (12 credit hour load) as assigned each semester in face-to-face, lecture-capture and/or web platforms. Candidates must be able to teach production and operations management at the undergraduate and graduate level; preference will be given to candidates who can also teach in other areas of business. Provide advising for undergraduate students (residential and distance students). Assist with development of new curriculum and assessment to support program-learning outcomes. Serve on departmental and university committees and perform other service activities as required. Develop appropriate scholarly activity as described in the FEC guidelines and faculty handbook, to include publishing in a peer reviewed journal. Contract is for nine (9) months. Work is primarily done on campus during the work week with an expectation of being physically at work and available to work with students. Regular and predictable attendance is required Other duties as assigned. Minimum Job Requirements: All candidates for this assistant professor position must have a terminal degree (Ph.D. or DBA) in a management discipline. ABD candidates may be considered. Candidates must be able to teach production and operations management at the undergraduate and graduate level; preference will be given to candidates who can also teach in other areas of business. Teaching experience in Web-based instruction and/or distance education is preferred. Industry experience is preferred. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: The position requires the ability to work effectively with a wide range of constituencies in a diverse community. Working Conditions Physical Demand and Working Conditions: Work is performed during normal work hours but may require some evening or weekend hours. Work is sedentary in nature and may require e xerting up to 25 pounds of force occasionally and/or a consistent amount of force frequently or constantly to lift, carry, push, pull or otherwise move objects. Work is primarily done on campus during the work week with an expectation of being physically at work and available to work with students. [As defined under the Americans with Disabilities Act, these include the aforementioned duties and responsibilities, minimum job requirements, knowledge, skills, and abilities, as well as physical demand and working conditions. This is not necessarily an all-inclusive listing.] Additional Information Date Available: January 2027 Application Review Date: Position is open until filled with review of applications beginning immediately. Conditions of Employment: Must pass a pre-employment background check. Electronic Application Instructions: Electronic applications may be submitted through the \"Apply\" link on the top of this page. Please attach the required documents to your electronic application. Required Documents: Brief letter of interest Curriculum vitae Evidence of online teaching and/or industry experience. Contact information for three references (at least one former or current supervisor), Transcripts (unofficial for application purposes). Equal Employment Opportunity /Title IX/IPRA. Eastern New Mexico University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, sex (including pregnancy, gender identity, and sexual orientation), age, disability, genetic information, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected under federal, state, or local laws. If a reasonable accommodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process, or to perform essential job functions, please contact the Office of Human Resources at (575) 562-2115. New Mexico is an open records state; therefore, ENMU complies with the Inspection of Public Records Act, NMSA 1978, Chapter 14, Article 2, from the Office of the New Mexico Attorney General. Any concerns regarding sex discrimination should be addressed to the Title IX Coordinator at either titleix.coordinator@enmu.eu , (575) 562-2235, or Curry Hall Office 127, 1500 S Avenue K, Portales, NM 88130. Requests for inspection of public records should be sent to planning.analysis@enmu.edu . For any other inquiries, please contact Human Resources at (575) 562-2115 or e-mail ENMU.HRrecruiter@enmu.edu . ENMU uses E-Verify to confirm the employment eligibility of all newly hired employees. To learn more about E-Verify, including your rights and responsibilities, please visit www.dhs.gov/E-Verify. Insurance Insurance for Eastern New Mexico University is offered through the New Mexico Public Schools Insurance Authority . High coverage and low coverage options are offered for medical and dental insurance so employees can choose the plan that’s right for them. Health insurance is offered through both Blue Cross and Blue Shield of New Mexico and the Presbyterian Health Plan Dental insurance is offered through United Concordia , Delta Dental , and Blue Cross Blue Shield Dental Vision insurance is offered through Davis Vision . Life insurance is offered through Standard Life Insurance Company and UNUM Life Insurance Company . Retirement Eastern New Mexico University participates with the New Mexico Educational Retirement Board (NMERB) , Social Security , and Medicare . The University also offers supplemental retirement plans. 403b and 457b plans are available through TIAA/CREF , AIG VALIC , Roth 403b and 457b plans are also available through TIAA/CREF . Paid Time Off Faculty will receive 5 personal days a year and 48 hours a semester for sick leave. Employee Educational Assistance Plan Eastern New Mexico University offers a tuition waiver for regular employees and retirees. This program waives the tuition for three courses (up to nine credit hours) per semester. Employees' spouses or children may be eligible to use the tuition waiver during any semester that it is not being used by the employee. 01 Ethical Conduct Section – Complaint with NM HB-128 Please type your name 02 Ethical Conduct Question (Compliant with NM HB-128) Please provide a list of current and former employers that were schools or that employed you in a position involving unsupervised contact with children or students. The list shall include the name, address, telephone number and other relevant contact information for each of the entities listed. 03 Ethical Conduct Question (Compliant with NM HB-128) Have you ever been under investigation for, or have been found to have violated, any state or federal statute relating to child abuse or neglect, sexual misconduct, or any sexual offense? Yes No 04 Ethical Conduct Question (Compliant with NM HB-128) Have you ever had a professional license or certificate denied, suspended, surrendered or revoked due to a finding of child abuse or ethical misconduct or while allegations of child abuse or ethical misconduct were pending or under investigation? Yes No 05 Ethical Conduct Question (Compliant with NM HB-128) Have you ever been under investigation for, or found to have violated, any ethical rule or policy approved by a former employer? Yes No 06 Ethical Conduct Question (Compliant with NM HB-128) By checking yes in this box, you authorize disclosure of information relevant to the ethical conduct questions and you authorize the release of related records by your previous employers, releasing them from any liability related to the disclosure or release of records. Yes No Required Question Employer Eastern New Mexico University Address 1500 S. Ave. K, Station 21 Portales, New Mexico, 88130 Phone 575-562-2115 Website http://www.enmu.edu Apply"
