    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/enmu/jobs/5495878/nursing-and-emgt-administrative-assistant": {
      "title": "Nursing and EMGT Administrative Assistant",
      "description": "Nursing and EMGT Administrative Assistant Salary Depends on Qualifications Location Main Campus - Portales, NM Job Type Full time permanent Job Number 2026-00167 Department Academic Affairs Division College of Liberal Arts and Sciences Opening Date 09/25/2026 Description Benefits Position Overview Position Summary: Under general supervision, perform a variety of office administrative and clerical functions for the department(s) on a regular basis. Requirements Duties and Responsibilities: Perform routine Administrative Assistant duties such as word processing, filing, verifying information, coordinating the flow of documents, and scheduling events and meetings. Enter data, compile and create reports, prepare letters, and general correspondence using Microsoft 365 software. Monitor the nursing and EMGT databases to confirm student information is current. Perform duties necessary to support the nursing scholarship program. Monitor departmental budget(s) and perform routine record keeping duties Perform a range of operational support activities for the department(s) and serve as a liaison with other departments on basic administrative and/or operational matters Greet and direct visitors, and when appropriate, resolve routine problems and answer inquiries concerning activities and operations of the department(s), accept, screen, and route telephone calls, and maintain a log of inquiries as required. Provide prospective student information and recruitment activities for the nursing and EMGT programs Order, stock, and distribute office supplies Organize and process student applications for admission into the BSN or MSN program May oversee the functional activities of student employees Support nursing and EMGT program staff and faculty in processing documents and following procedures relating to travel, purchase card transactions, leave, and other associated program activities Assist the Program Directors with workflow tasks Provide data and support to the Health and Human Services Chair as needed Regular and predictable attendance is required Perform other duties as assigned Minimum Job Requirements: High school diploma or GED certificate and a minimum of six months of experience directly related to the duties specified are required. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Ability to perform routine and moderately complex clerical tasks rapidly and accurately Skill in the use of standard office equipment Ability to understand and convey procedures and regulations established Ability to maintain confidentiality of records and information Ability to maintain web page content Skilled in use of Microsoft Office software (Word, Excel, PowerPoint, OneNote, Outlook) Ability to maintain an effective working relationship with others Ability to communicate effectively, both orally and in writing Ability to maintain confidentiality of records and informatio n based on FERPA and ENMU policies and guidelines Working Conditions Physical Demand and Working Conditions: Work is performed during normal work hours in an office setting but may require some evening or weekend hours. Work is sedentary in nature that at times requires exerting up to 25 pounds of force occasionally and/or a consistent amount of force frequently or constantly to lift, carry, push, pull, or otherwise move objects. Essential Functions: [As defined under the Americans with Disabilities Act, these include the aforementioned duties and responsibilities, minimum job requirements, knowledge, skills, and abilities, physical demands, and working conditions. This is not necessarily an all-inclusive listing.] Additional Information Condition of Employment: Must pass a pre-employment background check. Electronic Application Instructions: Electronic applications should be submitted through the \"Apply\" link at the top of this page. Please attach the following required documents to your electronic application: Required Documents: Letter of Interest Contact information for three references (blind or off-list reference checks may be conducted on finalists Please ensure that you attach all required documents, even if you have applied for other positions at ENMU, as the committee does not have access to those records. Equal Employment Opportunity /Title IX/IPRA. Eastern New Mexico University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, sex (including pregnancy, gender identity, and sexual orientation), age, disability, genetic information, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected under federal, state, or local laws. If a reasonable accommodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process, or to perform essential job functions, please contact the Office of Human Resources at (575) 562-2115. New Mexico is an open records state; therefore, ENMU complies with the Inspection of Public Records Act, NMSA 1978, Chapter 14, Article 2, from the Office of the New Mexico Attorney General. Any concerns regarding sex discrimination should be addressed to the Title IX Coordinator at either titleix.coordinator@enmu.eu , (575) 562-2235, or Curry Hall Office 127, 1500 S Avenue K, Portales, NM 88130. Requests for inspection of public records should be sent to planning.analysis@enmu.edu . For any other inquiries, please contact Human Resources at (575) 562-2115 or e-mail ENMU.HRrecruiter@enmu.edu . ENMU uses E-Verify to confirm the employment eligibility of all newly hired employees. To learn more about E-Verify, including your rights and responsibilities, please visit www.dhs.gov/E-Verify. Insurance Insurance for Eastern New Mexico University is offered through the New Mexico Public Schools Insurance Authority . High coverage and low coverage options are offered for medical and dental insurance so employees can choose the plan that’s right for them. Health insurance is offered through both Blue Cross and Blue Shield of New Mexico and the Presbyterian Health Plan Dental insurance is offered through United Concordia , Delta Dental , and Blue Cross Blue Shield Dental Vision insurance is offered through Davis Vision . Life insurance is offered through Standard Life Insurance Company and UNUM Life Insurance Company . Life insurance is offered through Standard Life Insurance Company and UNUM Life Insurance Company . Retirement Eastern New Mexico University participates with the New Mexico Educational Retirement Board (NMERB) , Social Security , and Medicare . The University also offers supplemental retirement plans. 403b and 457b plans are available through TIAA/CREF , AIG VALIC , Roth 403b and 457b plans are also available through TIAA/CREF . Paid Time Off During the first year of service, full time non-exempt (hourly) employees accrue 7 hours of annual leave and 7 hours of medical leave per month. During the second year of service, full time non-exempt employees accrue 10 hours of annual leave and 10 hours of medical leave per month. During the third and subsequent years of service, full time non-exempt employees accrue 14.66 hours of annual leave and 14 hours of medical leave per month. Employees must work for the University for three months before they are eligible to use annual leave. Temporary employees do not accrue leave. Employee Educational Assistance Plan Eastern New Mexico University offers a tuition waiver for regular employees and retirees. This program waives the tuition for three courses (up to nine credit hours) per semester. Employees' spouses or children may be eligible to use the tuition waiver during any semester that it is not being used by the employee. Employer Eastern New Mexico University Address 1500 S. Ave. K, Station 21 Portales, New Mexico, 88130 Phone 575-562-2115 Website http://www.enmu.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/enmu/jobs/5517123/library-technical-assistant-access-services": {
      "title": "Library Technical Assistant - Access Services",
      "description": "Library Technical Assistant - Access Services Salary Depends on Qualifications Location Main Campus - Portales, NM Job Type Full time permanent Job Number 2026-00174 Department Academic Affairs Division Golden Library Opening Date 10/14/2026 Description Benefits Questions Position Overview Position Summary: The Library Technical Assistant II – Access Services supports all aspects of Golden Library access services, including circulation, reserves, and interlibrary loan. This includes processing interlibrary borrowing and lending requests, stacks searching and document scanning and delivery, training and maintaining schedules for access services student workers, assisting with hold and overdue notices, stack maintenance, and library reserves services. This position reports to the Access Services Librarian. Requirements Duties and Responsibilities: Working in a team-oriented environment, the Library Technical Assistant II will: Respond to requests for physical and electronic copies of library materials, scan documents for electronic delivery. Perform searches for materials in an integrated library system and correctly interpret bibliographic data. Identify and retrieve library materials, including electronic journals. Correctly utilize and interpret bibliographic citations. Participate in hiring, training, and supervising access services student employees; assist with daily supervision, direction, and problem-solving. Communicate with other libraries via email and phone regarding bibliographic data, shipping, and other problems with lending requests and materials. Communicate with ENMU researchers in person and via email and phone to clarify ILL policies and procedures and to resolve problems concerning their ILL requests. Assist with maintaining circulation desk schedules for student workers; monitor advance requests, off/changes/gaps, and coordinate adjustments as needed, including coverage of the service desk. Process community borrower library cards. Perform stack maintenance, following established procedures and guidelines. Assist with searching for missing, claimed returned, and claimed lost items. Monitor and administer hold and overdue notices and checks/processes library materials. Maintain library reserves services. Troubleshoot and/or report system problems, as needed. Conduct data gathering for reports and create miscellaneous reports for the Access Services Librarian and other areas upon request; Contribute to Golden Library initiatives that further ENMU’s commitment to diversity and inclusion. Regular and predictable attendance required Perform other related duties and participate in special projects as assigned. Minimum Job Requirements: High school diploma or equivalent. Preferred Qualifications: Technical and customer service experience in a library. Experience working with access services, interlibrary loan, and/or document delivery in a library environment. Experience with ILLiad/Tipasa, OCLC, Docline, or other combination of bibliographic and/or ILL management systems. Experience with OCLC WorldShare or other integrated library system. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Evidence of strong attention to detail, problem-solving, analytical skills, and an ability to work with minimal direct supervision. Demonstrate initiative and proven ability to learn new technologies and adapt to change. Evidence of excellent oral, written, and interpersonal communication skills. Ability to manage and prioritize tasks and perform effectively in a fast-paced environment with a fluctuating workload and frequent distractions and interruptions. Sound judgment and ability to analyze information and solve problems within the scope of the job responsibilities. Strong customer service skills and commitment to providing service effectively in a diverse environment. Ability to initiate and maintain cooperative working relationships with co-workers, supervisors, and managers, and with other libraries. Ability to work harmoniously and as a team player, thrive in a team-based environment, and have skills in fostering teamwork among others. Demonstrated proficiency and capabilities with personal computers and standard computer office applications such as Microsoft Outlook, Word, Excel, Access, PowerPoint, or other productivity software, and with the Web, web searching, and virtual/webex meeting technologies. Knowledge of Library of Congress/Dewey Decimal/SUDOCS Classification system, authority and subject heading systems, and the use of bibliographic utilities. Knowledge of library access services procedures, database management, and use of technology in a technical services library environment. Working Conditions Physical Demand and Working Conditions: Work is performed during normal work hours. Work is sedentary in nature but at times requires exerting up to 25 pounds of force occasionally and/or a consistent amount of force frequently or constantly to lift, carry, push, pull, or otherwise move objects. Must be able to push heavy book trucks, move, and unpack boxes. Essential Functions: [As defined under the Americans with Disabilities Act, these include the aforementioned duties and responsibilities, minimum job requirements, knowledge, skills, and abilities, physical demands, and working conditions. This is not necessarily an all-inclusive listing.] Additional Information Application Review Date: Condition of Employment: Must pass a pre-employment background check. Electronic Application Instructions: Electronic applications should be submitted through the \"Apply\" link at the top of this page. Please attach the following required documents to your electronic application: Required Documents: Letter of Interest Contact information for three references (blind or off-list reference checks may be conducted on finalists Please ensure that you attach all required documents, even if you have applied for other positions at ENMU, as the committee does not have access to those records. Equal Employment Opportunity /Title IX/IPRA. Eastern New Mexico University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, sex (including pregnancy, gender identity, and sexual orientation), age, disability, genetic information, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected under federal, state, or local laws. If a reasonable accommodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process, or to perform essential job functions, please contact the Office of Human Resources at (575) 562-2115. New Mexico is an open records state; therefore, ENMU complies with the Inspection of Public Records Act, NMSA 1978, Chapter 14, Article 2, from the Office of the New Mexico Attorney General. Any concerns regarding sex discrimination should be addressed to the Title IX Coordinator at either titleix.coordinator@enmu.eu , (575) 562-2235, or Curry Hall Office 127, 1500 S Avenue K, Portales, NM 88130. Requests for inspection of public records should be sent to planning.analysis@enmu.edu . For any other inquiries, please contact Human Resources at (575) 562-2115 or e-mail ENMU.HRrecruiter@enmu.edu . ENMU uses E-Verify to confirm the employment eligibility of all newly hired employees. To learn more about E-Verify, including your rights and responsibilities, please visit www.dhs.gov/E-Verify . Insurance Insurance for Eastern New Mexico University is offered through the New Mexico Public Schools Insurance Authority . High coverage and low coverage options are offered for medical and dental insurance so employees can choose the plan that’s right for them. Health insurance is offered through both Blue Cross and Blue Shield of New Mexico and the Presbyterian Health Plan Dental insurance is offered through United Concordia , Delta Dental , and Blue Cross Blue Shield Dental Vision insurance is offered through Davis Vision . Life insurance is offered through Standard Life Insurance Company and UNUM Life Insurance Company . Life insurance is offered through Standard Life Insurance Company and UNUM Life Insurance Company . Retirement Eastern New Mexico University participates with the New Mexico Educational Retirement Board (NMERB) , Social Security , and Medicare . The University also offers supplemental retirement plans. 403b and 457b plans are available through TIAA/CREF , AIG VALIC , Roth 403b and 457b plans are also available through TIAA/CREF . Paid Time Off During the first year of service, full time non-exempt (hourly) employees accrue 7 hours of annual leave and 7 hours of medical leave per month. During the second year of service, full time non-exempt employees accrue 10 hours of annual leave and 10 hours of medical leave per month. During the third and subsequent years of service, full time non-exempt employees accrue 14.66 hours of annual leave and 14 hours of medical leave per month. Employees must work for the University for three months before they are eligible to use annual leave. Temporary employees do not accrue leave. Employee Educational Assistance Plan Eastern New Mexico University offers a tuition waiver for regular employees and retirees. This program waives the tuition for three courses (up to nine credit hours) per semester. Employees' spouses or children may be eligible to use the tuition waiver during any semester that it is not being used by the employee. 01 Ethical Conduct Section – Complaint with NM HB-128 Please type your name 02 Ethical Conduct Question (Compliant with NM HB-128) Have you ever been under investigation for, or found to have violated, any ethical rule or policy approved by a former employer? Yes No 03 Ethical Conduct Question (Compliant with NM HB-128) Have you ever been under investigation for, or have been found to have violated, any state or federal statute relating to child abuse or neglect, sexual misconduct, or any sexual offense? Yes No 04 Ethical Conduct Question (Compliant with NM HB-128) Have you ever had a professional license or certificate denied, suspended, surrendered or revoked due to a finding of child abuse or ethical misconduct or while allegations of child abuse or ethical misconduct were pending or under investigation? Yes No 05 Ethical Conduct Question (Compliant with NM HB-128) Please provide a list of current and former employers that were schools or that employed you in a position involving unsupervised contact with children or students. The list shall include the name, address, telephone number and other relevant contact information for each of the entities listed. 06 Ethical Conduct Question (Compliant with NM HB-128) By checking yes in this box, you authorize disclosure of information relevant to the ethical conduct questions and you authorize the release of related records by your previous employers, releasing them from any liability related to the disclosure or release of records. Yes No Required Question Employer Eastern New Mexico University Address 1500 S. Ave. K, Station 21 Portales, New Mexico, 88130 Phone 575-562-2115 Website http://www.enmu.edu Apply"
